# CO5300 QSPI Display Controller Configuration

config ELCO5300
	bool "CO5300 QSPI Display Controller"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_CHIPONE_ELCO5300_ENABLED
	help
	  Enable support for the CO5300 QSPI display controller.

config ELCO5300_TE_SYNC
	bool "Start frames on the panel's tearing-effect edge"
	depends on ELCO5300
	help
	  Enable the TE output (mode 1) and let a write that starts a frame
	  wait for the edge that begins a panel scan (the te-gpios property is
	  required). The write then stays behind the scan, so full-frame
	  updates do not tear. When a frame takes longer than one scan the
	  next frame waits for the following edge and the frame rate drops to
	  60/n FPS. The wait is skipped while the display is blanked, for
	  later areas of the same frame, and after repeated TE timeouts.

config ELCO5300_TE_WINDOW
	bool "Start every area inside its tear-free window"
	depends on ELCO5300_TE_SYNC
	help
	  Instead of waiting for the falling TE edge before a frame, start each
	  area (first, later and re-sent ones) at a phase of the panel's scan at
	  which the scan can neither overtake the write nor be overtaken by it
	  inside the area's rows. A full frame then starts up to several
	  milliseconds after an edge and stays on screen for one scan more
	  often than with the edge rule. Needs the scan period and the TE low
	  time measured (a few scans after start), a fresh edge and the normal
	  orientation; otherwise the edge rule is used. The window comes from
	  pure functions in co5300_te_window.h.

config ELCO5300_TE_WINDOW_MARGIN_US
	int "Margin around the forbidden start interval (microseconds)"
	default 500
	depends on ELCO5300_TE_WINDOW
	help
	  Added on both sides of an area's forbidden start interval, for the
	  start latency, the position of the first row against the edge and
	  the write time's tail beyond its recent maximum. It cannot cover a
	  long stall inside a write (a cooperative thread running for
	  milliseconds between two DMA pieces), which can tear the area; the
	  bench audit counts such a write as late. A stale edge falls back to
	  the edge rule.

config ELCO5300_STATS
	bool "CO5300 bench counters"
	depends on ELCO5300
	depends on SHELL
	help
	  Bench counters read by the app's ui_bench shell command; adds a few
	  cycles per transaction.
